    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328-a1">

                <pb facs="0373" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg339"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 181.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pringle to Mr. Munoz.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States, Guatemala and Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1897-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                1, 1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. Leon Aparicio, a duly naturalized
                    citizen of the United States, to whom I issued a passport on the 28th of
                    September, informs me that the Government of this Republic declines to recognize
                    him as a citizen of the United States.</p>
                <p>Mr. Leon Aparicio, having been born in France, and having renounced his
                    allegiance to the French Government, I think alters the case.</p>
                <p>Will you kindly inform me the reason of this action on the part of your
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. Lynch Pringle</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
